    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0480" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg412"/>

                <head>Mr. Ewing to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Légation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 30, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 31st ultimo, No. 12.</p>
                <p>Since my last despatch on the subject the rinderpest has virtually disappeared
                    from Holland. Still I would recommend that for many months to come the
                    precautions against its introduction from this country be continued.</p>
                <p>The authorities have arrived at the conclusion that the only effectual mode to
                    meet the pest is by prompt and unsparing slaughter of cattle in the vicinity
                    where it makes its appearance.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HUGH EWING.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
